Residential customers may receive and be entitled to levelized utility billing, from month to month, subject to and upon the following terms and conditions:
(1) Eligibility. Residential customers may receive and be entitled to levelized utility billing if:
a. They are residential customers receiving electric and/or water/sewer service;
b. Such customer has in writing exercised the option and elected to receive levelized billing;
c. Such customer has maintained an account for at least 12 months with no history of late payments; and
d. The General Government Administration Department shall concur in the delivery of levelized billing to the particular customer;
(2) The monthly levelized billing account will be calculated by the City averaging the current month's charges with all charges for utility services for the immediate past 11 months, excluding for both periods, fixed charges as defined herein, and taxes. All appropriate taxes will be billed based on the current month actual charges and late charges will be assessed.
(3) A penalty will not be charged to a customer on account balances. However, any levelized bill amount which is not paid by the due date will be subject to appropriate penalties. Refunds of credit balances will not be made except upon final billing. A customer may terminate eligibility for levelized billing at any time and at that time pay the balance due or receive the credit balance but in such event, the customer cannot elect to receive levelized billing for a period of at least 12 months from the date of termination;
(4) If a utility customer shall move to a location not serviced by the city, the balance owed by such customer or the credit due to the customer will be applied to the final bill. If the final billing results in a balance due to the customer, a refund check will be issued to the customer but if there is a balance due to the city, such balance shall be due in full and shall be paid by the due date reflected on the bill;
(5) If service to a customer shall be cut off or terminated for nonpayment, the account balance is due and must be paid prior to reconnection. Twelve consecutive months of service without termination for nonpayment shall be required before eligibility is restored;
(6) A utility customer transferring to another eligible location serviced by the city may continue on the levelized billing plan. The billing history of the new location will be used to calculate the level payment amount. If sufficient history is not available due to prolonged vacancy or because the account is new, only the available monthly charges will be averaged and if no history is available, the first month's bill will be the actual charges and averaging will commence with the second month; and
(7) Fixed charges as used herein means contributions to the share program, garbage collection fees and security light fees.
(Code 1998, § 74-11; Ord. No. 20-98, 12-7-1998; Ord. No. 02-2011, 4-4-2011)

